## 🧪 Benchmarking

The template includes a benchmarking system to evaluate channel finder performance.

### Run Benchmarks

```bash
# Run all enabled benchmarks
uv run python -m {{ package_name }}.services.channel_finder.benchmarks.cli

# Run first 10 queries only
uv run python -m {{ package_name }}.services.channel_finder.benchmarks.cli --queries 0:10

# Use different model
uv run python -m {{ package_name }}.services.channel_finder.benchmarks.cli --model anthropic/claude-sonnet
```

### Benchmark Results

Results are saved to `data/benchmarks/results/` with detailed metrics:
- Success rate
- Average latency per query
- Exact match vs partial match rates
- Individual query performance
- Model usage costs (if available)

### Adding Custom Benchmarks

The default benchmark uses the tier-resolved query set at
`data/benchmarks/queries.json` (one file, read by every paradigm). To run a
custom query set, write a new file alongside it and point
`channel_finder.benchmark.dataset_path` at it:

```json
[
  {
    "user_query": "beam current channel",
    "targeted_pv": ["SR:DIAG:DCCT:01:CURRENT:RB"],
    "category": "single"
  }
]
```

```yaml
channel_finder:
  benchmark:
    dataset_path: data/benchmarks/my_custom.json
```

